# Alembic Migrations — الخلاقي

## Commands

# Create a new migration (auto-detect changes)
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add user_email column"

# Apply all pending migrations
alembic upgrade head

# Rollback one migration
alembic downgrade -1

# See current revision
alembic current

# See history
alembic history --verbose

# Stamp DB with a revision without running it
alembic stamp head

## Notes

- `env.py` reads `DATABASE_URL` from environment (via app.config).
- In production, always run `alembic upgrade head` before starting the app.
- For SQLite dev, use `alembic revision --autogenerate` after model changes.
